  "id": "COMPOUND:523 - PROTEIN:1084",
  "verbalization": "Ciprofloxacin is implicated in the regulation of Lysozyme through a multi-step pathway involving Serum paraoxonase/arylesterase 1. This enzyme is targeted by Amonafide and eteplirsen, both of which have a direct relationship with Lysozyme. The evidence suggests that ciprofloxacin may influence the activity of Serum paraoxonase/arylesterase 1, potentially modulating the function of Lysozyme. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which ciprofloxacin could indirectly affect Lysozyme, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores support a consistent link between ciprofloxacin and Lysozyme through these intermediaries, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct or indirect relationship.",
